  "fields": {
    "responsibility": "One complete lifecycle-owned binding-read replacement: context admission, atomic shared fixup publication, generated reads, cooperative freeze/restore and last-entry drain.",
    "retired": "Repeated raw-native owner proof in admitted generated primitive reads; the baseline early-DONE fixup publication is replaced by explicit claim/ready/refused states. Rejected prototype arrays, per-host hook, module/directory cache and duplicate permit/epoch are removed; public raw native services remain checked.",
    "validation": "Current source native build;37 selected framework tests; real Make PBT12 histories240 actions, processor1 history8 actions and observer control13to1 replay; globals27216/426pages; actual multi-shot18frames36wide roots; GSC2387checks306fixtures290layout15plans and C102cases; actual failed-module load and old-module refusal; fixup TLC41distinct140generated0queued and6 protocol/control tests. Original default frame failures and GSI393/408 versus baseline392/408 remain failures; no candidate-only failing GSI case.",
    "benefits": "Explicit executable-publication correctness and source-level work elimination: generated reads consume retained context ownership and use one canonical primitive page lookup. One native VM identity supports the context/runtime boundary without caching moving Scheme values. Timing is mixed and not a stable general speedup.",
    "costs": "Context+8 bytes per configured slot, module+8 bytes, this-profile global state+512 bytes; unchanged heap/watchdogs and no additional per-binding allocator. Final published-source p1 medians: request -2.299%, composed +0.298%, overlapping samples; no universal, cold-build or whole-SMP performance claim.",
    "process": "One complete21-file post-foundation REV, not setter fragments. Main foundation checkpoint4/4 and independent branch checkpoint1/12 remain distinct and unchanged. Remaining68-path pre-commit queue is classified by SysML; shared/unqualified hunks remain outside.",
    "checklist": "dev/refactoring/modern-c/binding-activation.org#binding-activation",
    "models": "Strict OpenSysML SDK and independent native projection drive shared ASCENT. New fixup QNT alone covers publication interleavings; existing entry/unload QNT and Lean root/representation laws retain separate duties. Reviewed conditional C refinement is not a machine-checked C memory-model proof.",
    "open": "Default-SMP and whole-family failures remain; no full current Gerbil rebuild, live cross-VM context migration or complete CFFI acceptance. Partial name interning may remain after failed setup; only executable descriptor authority is withheld. Stable runtime net speedup is unproved. New fixed metadata and code-layout sensitivity remain explicit."
  },
